-- title:
--   Frobenius conjugate of a smooth A-point of X
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a nonzero $M$ with $p \mid M$ and $M/p \neq 0$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb Z/M)^\times$, and assume $j$ lies in the field $\mathrm{qExpFunctionFieldC}\ \mathbb Q\ \top$ generated by ratios of integral $q$-expansions at full level; let $\mathfrak X$ be a model bundle `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $p$ a nonunit of $A$, whose residue field $\kappa$ is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$, and let $\rho : R\,p \to A$ be a ring map whose composite with $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$ is the structure map. Let $\mathrm{frob}$ be a semilinear automorphism of the level-$\Gamma_N$ $q$-expansion field over $\kappa$ (a compatible pair of ring automorphisms of the field and of $\kappa$) acting coefficientwise by $x \mapsto x^p$ on Laurent coefficients. Assume $p = 0$ on the $\kappa$-fibres at levels $\Gamma_N$ and $\Gamma_M$, and let $\theta_N$, $\theta_M$ be endomorphisms of those fibres whose composites with the first projection equal that of the absolute Frobenius `frobenius p 1` and whose composites with the second projection are that projection (relative Frobenius over $\kappa$). Assume (i) for every closed point $P$ of $(\mathfrak X.\mathrm{Mfib}\,A\,h_A\,\rho\,h_\rho).C$ the point obtained by transporting $\theta_N$ through `𝔛.efib` and its inverse is closed, with place $\mathrm{frob} \cdot \mathrm{placeOfPoint}\,P$; (ii) $\mathrm{Fr} \in \mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ lies in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ and induces on $\kappa$ the map $a \mapsto a^p$. Given $i \in \{0,1\}$, a section $y$ of $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{Meta}.\mathrm{toBase}$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a morphism $u : \mathrm{Spec}\,A \to X\,p\,(\Gamma_M M H)\,hj$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,\rho$ whose generic restriction is $y$ via `𝔛.eeta` and whose image lies in $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{smoothLocus}$, a special point $u_\kappa$ of $u$ (a section of the second projection of the $\kappa$-fibre whose first projection is $\mathrm{Spec}(\mathrm{residue}) \circ u$), and a closed point $P$ with $(\mathfrak X.\mathrm{efib} \ggg \mathfrak X.\mathrm{comp}\,i)(P) = u_\kappa(\text{closed point})$, and assuming $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{comp}\,i$ intertwines $\theta_N$ and $\theta_M$ at that point, the conclusion asserts the existence of $y'$ and $u'$ with $u'$ equal to $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the automorphism of $A$ induced by $\mathrm{Fr}$ followed by $u$, with generic restriction $y'$, image again in the smooth locus, $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{Meta}.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}\,y' = \mathrm{arithmeticGalois}(\mathrm{Fr}) \cdot \mathfrak X.\mathrm{Meta}.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}\,y$, and with a special point $u_\kappa' = u_\kappa$ followed by $\theta_M$ satisfying the same two projection identities, together with a closed point $P'$ lying over $u_\kappa'$ under $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{efib} \ggg \mathfrak X.\mathrm{comp}\,i$ and with $\mathrm{placeOfPoint}\,P' = \mathrm{frob} \cdot \mathrm{placeOfPoint}\,P$.
--
--   This is the compatibility, for a point of the model lying in the smooth locus over a place of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ above $p$, between conjugation by a Frobenius element of the decomposition group at the generic level, the coefficientwise $p$-power action on places of the $q$-expansion function field, and the relative Frobenius on the characteristic-$p$ fibre, with the index $i$ of the component unchanged. It feeds the computation of the Frobenius twist of a point of the Néron-type object attached to $J_H$ at $p$ in [`ModularCurve.JHNeronObjectAtP.ptsSp_symm_frobeniusTwist_eq_glueMap_of_pointReduction`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JHNeronObjectAtP.ptsSp_symm_frobeniusTwist_eq_glueMap_of_pointReduction).
